---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { pageTitle, SITE_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../lib/seo';

const description = `How ${SITE_NAME} handles your data. Briefly: it does not collect any.`;
---
<BaseLayout title={pageTitle('Privacy')} description={description}>
  <div class="wrap section prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>
      This site is a set of static files. It sets no cookies, asks for nothing, and has
      no login, no comments and no forms.
    </p>

    <h2>There is no contact form</h2>
    <p>
      Getting in touch is a plain <code>mailto:</code> link to
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>, which opens your own mail
      client. Nothing you type is submitted to this site, because there is nothing here
      to submit it to.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      If page-view counting is enabled, it is done with a privacy-preserving analytics
      script that stores no cookie, creates no cross-site identifier and records no
      personal data. There is nothing here that needs a consent banner, and this page
      has to keep being able to say that.
    </p>

    <h2>What your browser reaches</h2>
    <p>
      Pages here link out — to Manning, to LinkedIn, to Bluesky. Following one of those
      takes you to somebody else’s site under somebody else’s policy. Fonts and images
      are served from this site rather than from a third party, so simply reading a page
      contacts nobody else.
    </p>

    <h2>Server logs</h2>
    <p>
      The host that serves these files keeps ordinary web-server logs, which include IP
      addresses, for a short period and for the purpose of running the server.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
